source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira renders the whole of `(flagoff)` as one grey flag icon, so it is a token of its own; jiro reads it as an emoticon directive.
-- input.jira --
(flagoff)
-- rendered.html --
<p><img class="emoticon" src="/jira/images/icons/emoticons/flag_grey.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/></p>
-- want.md --
:emoticon[(flagoff)]
-- warnings.json --
[]
